WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:06.370
Two names stand above all others in the annals
of all-time action stars — Sylvester Stallone

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.200
and Arnold Schwarzenegger.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:13.440
Both men are icons whose careers started very
differently, but ended up following remarkably

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.969
similar paths.

00:00:14.969 --> 00:00:19.110
It's no easy task deciding who's ultimately
better, but we're going to try.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:24.700
This titanic battle wouldn't be so tough to
call if Stallone and Schwarzenegger didn't

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.320
have so much in common.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.520
For starters, each guy headlined some of the
best action movies of their era.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.750
They also played some of the most famous characters
in film.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:39.750
For Stallone, there's perpetual underdog boxer
Rocky Balboa and the PTSD-stricken, one-man

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.400
army John Rambo.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:46.750
For Schwarzenegger, there's the killer robot
from the future, the T-800 from The Terminator

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:52.500
franchise, the Predator-killing Major Dutch,
and the sword-wielding Conan the Barbarian.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.260
Given their similarities, it's no wonder they
had a heated public rivalry for years.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:02.149
From Schwarzenegger throwing shade in movies
like Twins and to Stallone literally throwing

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:06.990
a giant bowl of flowers at Arnold during the
Golden Globes, it's clear that during their

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:09.530
heydays, the two couldn't stand each other.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:13.600
While they're friends today, you better believe
their rivalry still exists low-key.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:19.720
Sylvester Stallone is mostly associated with
shoot-'em-up, one-man army action movies,

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:23.820
which even at their best have never really
been associated with high art.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:28.620
Nevertheless, Stallone does boast artistic
bona fides that Schwarzenegger does not.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:33.360
In fact, Stallone has achieved the pinnacle
of Hollywood's artistic accomplishments — the

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.110
Academy Award.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:39.390
Stallone has been nominated for the Academy
Awards three times – for Best Actor and

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:45.530
Best Original Screenplay for Rocky in 1977,
and for Best Supporting Actor for Creed in

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:46.670
2016.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:51.700
This makes him one of only six actors to be
nominated more than once for playing the same

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:55.810
character, alongside Cate Blanchett, Paul
Newman, and Al Pacino.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:01.400
While Stallone didn't win Best Actor or Best
Screenplay, Rocky ultimately won the Academy

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:02.420
Award for Best Picture.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:07.700
Though Stallone has Schwarzenegger beat when
it comes to cinematic awards, Arnold surely

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:11.400
takes the cake when it comes to non-cinematic
awards.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:16.610
Schwarzenegger is a world-class athlete who's
considered one of, if not the, greatest bodybuilders

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:17.810
of all time.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:21.730
In many ways, he's the Michael Jordan or Tiger
Woods of his sport.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:25.980
While experts can quibble about who's the
best based on this stat or that, nobody can

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:31.599
deny that Schwarzenegger brought more attention
to bodybuilding than anybody before or since.

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:36.850
That said, Arnold's career isn't just hype
— he truly was the real deal.

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:42.200
From the time he first picked up a barbell
back home in Austria at 13 years old to finally

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:49.040
hanging up his speedo in 1980 at the ripe
old age of 33, Schwarzenegger won over 20

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:54.540
bodybuilding championships, including three
Mr. Universes, and seven Mr. Olympias.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:03:00.410
Along the way, he literally wrote the book
on bodybuilding, 1977's Arnold: The Education

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.599
of a Bodybuilder.

00:03:02.709 --> 00:03:04.819
Arnold Schwarzenegger can't stay still.

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:08.910
He's conquered bodybuilding, Hollywood, and
California politics.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:12.870
When it comes to his actual acting skills
though, he's never really worked to better

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:16.220
them, as his screen presence is powered by
sheer charisma.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:17.240
"Oh, excuse me.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:18.660
I forgot to tell you.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.830
This is my ferret."

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:26.190
Stallone not only takes his acting more seriously,
but he also has plenty of clout for offscreen

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.190
work.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:31.720
In addition to being nominated for the Academy
Award twice for playing Rocky Balboa, he also

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:38.019
delivered a powerful performance as a PTSD-stricken
Vietnam vet in First Blood, and he even stole

00:03:38.019 --> 00:03:44.159
the show from Robert De Niro, Harvey Keitel,
and Ray Liotta in James Mangold's criminally

00:03:44.159 --> 00:03:46.580
under-appreciated Cop Land.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:51.100
Stallone is also accomplished off-camera,
having screenplay credits on more than 25

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:54.769
TV shows or movies, and directing credits
for eight films.

00:03:54.769 --> 00:04:00.549
Sure, some of his creative efforts are genuinely
horrible -- such as 1983's Saturday Night

00:04:00.549 --> 00:04:06.860
Fever sequel Staying Alive, which earned 0%
on Rotten Tomatoes -- but hey, even Spielberg

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:08.900
and Scorsese have had duds.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:14.379
With several Rocky, Rambo, and Expendables
films in his oeuvre, Stallone is an accomplished

00:04:14.379 --> 00:04:20.699
and bankable action director, with $1.3 billion
in global grosses for just eight films.

00:04:21.979 --> 00:04:27.589
Besides being one of only a few movie stars
who started his career as a world-class athlete,

00:04:27.589 --> 00:04:31.669
Schwarzenegger boasts another — arguably
even more impressive — accomplishment.

00:04:31.669 --> 00:04:35.509
He's one of only three actors to become governor
of a state.

00:04:35.509 --> 00:04:39.550
Schwarzenegger was elected to succeed the
recalled Democrat Gray Davis, serving as the

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:44.259
Republican governor of California from 2003-2011.

00:04:44.259 --> 00:04:49.710
Schwarzenegger told The Hollywood Reporter
he also would've run for president in 2016,

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:54.830
but he was unable to because the Constitution
forbids foreign-born people from serving as

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:55.830
president.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:59.990
The only other actor-governor left to mention
is Schwarzenegger's memorable Predator co-star

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:06.160
Jesse Ventura, who served as governor of Minnesota
from 1999-2003.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:10.629
While Stallone would win our vote if he ran
for pretty much anything, only Schwarzenegger

00:05:10.629 --> 00:05:14.020
has served as governor of America's most populous
state.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:18.020
Star power is hard to quantify, or even define.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:23.029
You could be the most talented actor, the
most beautiful person, or the most charismatic

00:05:23.029 --> 00:05:27.589
performer, but that's no guarantee anybody
is going to buy a ticket to watch your movie.

00:05:27.589 --> 00:05:31.340
Whatever star power is, you either have it,
or you don't.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:33.689
Stallone and Schwarzenegger both do, in spades.

00:05:33.689 --> 00:05:35.129
But who has more?

00:05:35.129 --> 00:05:39.430
There's really only one signifier that matters
in Hollywood — who's made more money at

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:40.529
the box office.

00:05:40.529 --> 00:05:44.180
By that standard, the winner is clearly Stallone.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:51.129
Stallone's career box office total is $2.8
billion domestic and $6.3 billion worldwide,

00:05:51.129 --> 00:05:56.659
beating out Schwarzenegger's career total
of $2.1 billion domestic and $5.4 billion

00:05:56.659 --> 00:05:58.059
worldwide.

00:05:58.059 --> 00:06:02.840
As massive as those numbers are, they're even
more impressive when you consider they aren't

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:08.370
adjusted for inflation, as both actor's biggest
hits happened more than 25 years ago.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:14.339
Worth noting, Stallone has been in more movies,
62 films to Schwarzenegger's 44, and Arnold

00:06:14.339 --> 00:06:19.289
dropped out of acting while serving as California's
governor from 2003-2011.

00:06:19.289 --> 00:06:25.210
However, by that point, both actors were past
their primes as box office draws, so it's

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:29.249
unlikely Schwarzenegger would've starred in
a massive hit during those years.

00:06:29.249 --> 00:06:35.050
In fact, his last pre-political role was a
supporting part in the Jackie Chan bomb Around

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:36.539
the World in 80 Days.

00:06:37.539 --> 00:06:42.789
Though Stallone's box office total beats Schwarzenegger's,
Arnold takes the cake when it comes to average

00:06:42.789 --> 00:06:43.789
earnings.

00:06:43.789 --> 00:06:49.710
Stallone's 62 films have earned an average
of $54 million domestically and $112 million

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:55.939
worldwide, while Schwarzenegger's 44 movies
have brought home an average of $60 million

00:06:55.939 --> 00:06:59.659
domestically and $135 million worldwide.

00:06:59.659 --> 00:07:04.219
While both guys found their greatest success
playing their marquee characters -- Stallone

00:07:04.219 --> 00:07:09.729
with Rocky and Rambo and Schwarzenegger with
the T-800, they were also successful in other

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:13.069
roles, proving neither man was a one-hit character
wonder.

00:07:13.069 --> 00:07:15.979
So, which matters more — totals or averages?

00:07:15.979 --> 00:07:19.580
You'll have to ask the accountants at the
movie studios about that.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:24.539
All we can say is that during their commercial
peaks, Stallone and Schwarzenegger were money.

00:07:25.539 --> 00:07:30.009
You can compare Stallone and Schkwarzenegger
on several tangible, measurable fronts -- from

00:07:30.009 --> 00:07:35.629
box office results to career accomplishments
to the size of their respective pecs and biceps.

00:07:35.629 --> 00:07:38.729
But there are some metrics where you have
to just go with your heart.

00:07:38.729 --> 00:07:43.840
Therefore, we can confidently say that Stallone's
most famous characters, Rocky and Rambo, are

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:47.039
more iconic than Schwarzenegger's, the T-800.

00:07:47.039 --> 00:07:49.110
This is subjective, but defensible.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:54.610
For one, Rocky is the winner of three Academy
Awards, including Best Picture, and it spearheaded

00:07:54.610 --> 00:08:01.249
an eight-film franchise, including the Creed
movies, with $1.5 billion in global box office.

00:08:01.249 --> 00:08:05.739
While the Rambo films are less critically
acclaimed than Rocky, the five-film franchise

00:08:05.739 --> 00:08:10.610
has still earned an impressive $817 million
over five films.

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:16.599
Yes, The Terminator franchise has earned more
-- $2 billion worldwide over six films -- but

00:08:16.599 --> 00:08:21.819
one film, Terminator: Salvation, didn't even
star Schwarzenegger, while the last film,

00:08:21.819 --> 00:08:24.419
Terminator: Dark Fate, bombed big time.

00:08:24.419 --> 00:08:28.419
None of the Rocky or Rambo movies have ever
performed poorly -- whether we're talking

00:08:28.419 --> 00:08:30.869
about the box office or review scores.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:35.979
Schwarzenegger's biggest hit outgrossed Stallone's
by a pretty substantial margin.

00:08:35.979 --> 00:08:41.630
With $204 million domestic, Terminator 2:
Judgment Day was the biggest box office hit

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.639
in 1991.

00:08:43.639 --> 00:08:51.160
Stallone achieved a similar feat in 1976 when
Rocky topped the box office with $117 million,

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:58.120
and he almost did the same thing in 1985 when
Rambo: First Blood Part II earned $150 million

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:02.180
and Rocky IV earned $127 million.

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:06.660
Impressive achievements all around, but Stallone's
biggest hit -- not adjusted for inflation

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:09.550
-- isn't even a Rocky or Rambo movie.

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:14.990
Excluding his cameo in Guardians of the Galaxy
Vol. 2, Stallone's biggest grosser is the

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:21.040
$311 million worldwide that The Expendables
2 earned in 2012.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:27.910
Not bad, but still less than $200 million
of what T2 earned worldwide 20 years earlier.

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:33.089
Besides, Schwarzenegger also had a prominent
role in Stallone's biggest hit, The Expendables

00:09:33.089 --> 00:09:34.089
2.

00:09:34.089 --> 00:09:35.260
Talk about bragging rights!

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:40.459
Part of being a successful movie star isn't
just thriving during the big hits — it's

00:09:40.459 --> 00:09:42.519
surviving the big bombs.

00:09:42.519 --> 00:09:46.910
One thing we can say for Sylvester Stallone
is that he didn't star in one of the most

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:51.459
significant bombs in Hollywood history, Batman
&amp; Robin.

00:09:51.459 --> 00:09:56.920
Schwarzenegger did, but we doubt he regrets
that decision, as he netted a cool $25 million

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:58.460
for playing Mr. Freeze.

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:03.620
We think $25 million for less than one month's
work was a worthy price to pay for killing

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:08.629
the Batman franchise, though we doubt Warner
Brothers was too pleased with the investment.

00:10:08.629 --> 00:10:14.460
Ironically, Batman &amp; Robin is actually not
Schwarzenegger's worst movie -- see The Villain,

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:19.930
which earned a horrid 0% Tomatometer score
-- but it is his most notorious.

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:25.230
It's also one of the most influential superhero
movies of all time, and not in a good way,

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:30.270
as it ended one of the biggest hit franchises
ever, the Burton-Schumacher Batman films.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:35.260
Plus, it sent the Dark Knight into exile until
Christopher Nolan brought him back eight years

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:37.730
later in Batman Begins.

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:42.319
Stallone has some stinkers, no doubt, but
he's never killed a multi-billion franchise

00:10:42.319 --> 00:10:44.270
and still made millions doing it.

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:48.519
As Rocky tells his son in 2006's Rocky Balboa:

00:10:48.519 --> 00:10:51.220
"It ain't about how hard you can hit.

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:54.930
It's about how hard you can get hit and keep
moving forward.

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:58.250
How much you can take and keep moving forward."

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:03.149
Make no mistake, moviegoers and critics gave
Stallone a stiff right hook to the jaw with

00:11:03.149 --> 00:11:05.649
the 1992 comedy Stop!

00:11:05.649 --> 00:11:07.079
Or My Mom Will Shoot.

00:11:07.079 --> 00:11:13.930
With a 7% critic's score and 21% audience
score on Rotten Tomatoes and $26.6 million

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:17.730
worldwide, it's Stallone's biggest career
misfire.

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:24.000
Yes, with a 4% Tomatometer score, Reach Me
is technically his worst movie, but that ensemble

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:29.339
dramedy was a misguided if noble defeat that
only saw limited release in 2014.

00:11:29.339 --> 00:11:30.339
Stop!

00:11:30.339 --> 00:11:32.990
Or My Mom Will Shoot was supposed to be a
hit!

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:34.699
What was Stallone thinking?

00:11:34.699 --> 00:11:36.900
Turns out, it was Schwarzenegger.

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:41.839
According to a Q&amp;A on Instagram, Stallone
claimed Schwarzenegger tricked him into doing

00:11:41.839 --> 00:11:45.079
the part by making Stallone think he was interested.

00:11:45.079 --> 00:11:47.960
He wasn't, and it's easy to see why.

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:53.459
While Schwarzenegger had success in action-comedies
like Twins, Kindergarten Cop, and Jingle All

00:11:53.459 --> 00:11:58.879
the Way, Stallone's biggest failure was in
trying to beat Arnold at his own game.

00:11:58.879 --> 00:12:02.800
Stallone learned the hard way, you don't play
politics with Schwarzenegger.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:06.350
It's one of the most coveted places in all
of Hollywood.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:10.949
More than a table at Musso and Frank's or
courtside seats next to Jack Nicholson at

00:12:10.949 --> 00:12:14.459
a Los Angeles Lakers home game, it's top billing.

00:12:14.459 --> 00:12:19.470
To be listed first above the movie's title
is an absolute statement about star power,

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:24.069
and so naturally, it's inspired numerous squabbles
among movie stars.

00:12:24.069 --> 00:12:28.769
When it comes to our two actors in question,
Sylvester Stallone has always gotten top billing

00:12:28.769 --> 00:12:30.779
over Arnold Schwarzenegger.

00:12:30.779 --> 00:12:35.949
This wasn't a surprise in The Expendables,
as Arnold had an uncredited cameo, while Stallone

00:12:35.949 --> 00:12:38.459
wrote, directed, and starred in it.

00:12:38.459 --> 00:12:43.540
Stallone again got top billing in The Expendables
2 and The Expendables 3, while Arnold got

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:48.749
an "and Schwarzenegger" credit, a respectable
position given his minor supporting role.

00:12:48.749 --> 00:12:54.759
But in 2013's Escape Plan, with just Stallone
and Schwarzenegger as above-the-title leads,

00:12:54.759 --> 00:12:55.939
Stallone got top billing.

00:12:55.939 --> 00:13:02.639
Sure, the movie bombed with $103 million worldwide
on a $70 million budget, but that's beside

00:13:02.639 --> 00:13:03.639
the point.

00:13:03.639 --> 00:13:06.779
When it comes to billing, Stallone has always
come out on top.

00:13:07.779 --> 00:13:11.959
We've compared and contrasted Stallone and
Schwarzenegger in quite a few ways, but one

00:13:11.959 --> 00:13:13.899
important one still remains.

00:13:13.899 --> 00:13:15.020
Who would win in a fight?

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:19.460
It may not be the most mature way to settle
the debate, but it makes the most sense, given

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:22.449
they're both men whose brands are built on
machismo.

00:13:22.449 --> 00:13:24.990
If we're being honest, Schwarzenegger would
win.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:30.790
For one, Stallone's billed height of 5'10"
is well below Schwarzenegger's 6'2".

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:35.920
And while Stallone is pretty jacked, Schwarzenegger
is one of the greatest bodybuilders of all

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:36.920
time.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.020
Additionally, Arnold was known for his size
and strength.

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:45.209
Sure, Stallone was Rocky Balboa, but convincingly
playing a world-class athlete isn't the same

00:13:45.209 --> 00:13:46.430
as being one.

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:50.520
While we'd never want to see them actually
fight, if it ever came time to throw hands,

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:52.080
our money's on Arnold.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:54.769
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:13:54.769 --> 00:13:59.559
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
action stars are coming soon.

